        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ba2dbe84-7b9a-559c-add3-04deba43066a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick Carpentier\n- Companies: Ford, Go FAS Racing\n- Products: Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, Mercury Milan\n- Events: 1997 CART season\n- Concepts: Rookie of the Year, NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, CD3 platform\n- Places: Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Carpentier was born on August 13, 1971, and he is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\n- Patrick Carpentier was the Rookie of the Year in the 1997 CART season.\n- The Ford Fusion was introduced for the 2006 model year.\n- The Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant alongside its rebadged variant the Lincoln MKZ.\n- The discontinued Mercury Milan was formerly a rebadged variant of the Ford Fusion.\n- The Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, and Mercury Milan share the CD3 platform.\n- Patrick Carpentier currently competes part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series.\n- Patrick Carpentier drives the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series.",
